        "problem": "Identify the surface $4{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8x+8z+4=0.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8x+8z+4 & =0 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)+8{y}^{2}+2({z}^{2}+4z)+4 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]+8{y}^{2}+2[(z+2)^{2}-4]+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{8{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{2(z+2)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $(1,0,-2).$",
